  "text": "With Bowers out in a soft matchup against Miami, Michael Mayer is a borderline TE1 this weekend.\n\nMoved the Raiders pass-catchers up, Tre Tucker feels like a relatively solid flex and Nailor startable in deeper leagues.\n\nFor Jeanty, this should be a theoretical increase to his pass-catching upside, but I do worry about offensive efficiency/TD opps in a Bowers-less offense. That environment issue doesn't bother me in Week 1 against a bad Miami defense, but would have some concern if this injury became a bit longer-term.",
