 {
  "type": "tweet",
  "id": "2097449702673224162",
  "url": "https://x.com/ffdataroma/status/2097449702673224162",
  "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ffdataroma/status/2097449702673224162",
  "text": "Have a feeling this will get a lot of negative comments, but the current narrative around Baker is confusing to me. \n\nPrior to the injuries piling up in the middle of 2025, Baker had been one of the most efficient QBs in football for the past few years. See his adjusted net yds/attempt (ANY/A) since 2023, per @FantasyPtsData:\n\n2023: 6.47 (12th/30 QBs)\n2024: 7.13 (8th/31 QBs)\n2025 (Wk1-6): 8.10 (4th/30 QBs)\n2025 (Wk7 on): 4.88 (28th/31 QBs)\n\nNot only was Baker dealing with countless injuries last year, his top O-lineman and receivers were either playing banged up or inactive as well.\n\nIMO, a capable enough QB to get paid/try to make a run with, and an extremely obvious bounce-back candidate.",
