 {
  "type": "tweet",
  "id": "2095603638676689386",
  "url": "https://x.com/ffdataroma/status/2095603638676689386",
  "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/ffdataroma/status/2095603638676689386",
  "text": "Since 2023, 14 WRs have an aDOT of 15+ yards downfield. 13 of those WRs sit at a 0.16 targets per route run (TPRR) or lower. \n\nThe remaining WR is Christian Watson, who has a 0.23 TPRR (!) in this time, per @FantasyPtsData.\n\nWatson is poised for the biggest role of his career. Seems like a very good chance we see a notably lower aDOT this year, and in turn a higher TPRR (like his rookie year, 14.0 aDOT and 0.27 TPRR). \n\nWhile the deep shots allow for splash plays, an aDOT this high (17.6 L3 years) ultimately caps Watson's target ceiling and therefore fantasy upside, so it would be beneficial to get some more short/intermediate looks as opposed to low-percentage deeper passes.",
  "fullText": "Since 2023, 14 WRs have an aDOT of 15+ yards downfield. 13 of those WRs sit at a 0.16 targets per route run (TPRR) or lower. \n\nThe remaining WR is Christian Watson, who has a 0.23 TPRR (!) in this time, per @FantasyPtsData.\n\nWatson is poised for the biggest role of his career.",
